WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
<b>March 1st, 2020</b>

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.680
We've been working with the power 
companies and communications services,

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>Saga Prefectural Office Special Task Force HQ</b>

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.980
and they've gotten cellular service and 
web access back up in certain areas.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.740
How long does it look like it'll 
take for the entire prefecture?

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.680
There's still no real way to tell...

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.220
Since transportation is so limited, 
it puts a damper on repairs.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.610
Where are we at in terms 
of estimating the damage?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.270
The areas that have 
reestablished communications

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.490
have been reporting their casualties 
and evacuation status,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:28.000
along with damage to residential 
areas and transport infrastructure.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.080
We need an accurate assessment 
as quickly as possible.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.250
There's been flooding 
throughout the prefecture,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.840
but it looks like it's been most severe in 
the north and the Sajiro and Sanshin areas.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.440
The water itself is gradually 
starting to recede, but...

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.140
It's still too early to 
make any real estimations.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
Watch for any additional problems 
the initial damage might cause.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.140
I'll coordinate with the JSDF, fire services,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.230
and the Social Welfare Council to try 
to deal with things as they develop.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:50.010
Please do.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.190
Governor! I need to speak with you! Please!

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.020
Stop that!

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.320
You have to put a rush on getting the 
infrastructure around the Tosu area back up!

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.930
Isn't Tosu a critical intersection 
for land-based transport in Kyushu?!

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.470
We should move you to a 
different room to be safe.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.460
Getting transportation back up means 
everything else will be that much faster!

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.550
We're fully aware of that.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.720
This isn't the kind of thing we 
need a civilian perspective on.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.040
I'm asking you to do this
for the sake of Saga's future!

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.880
Get him out of here, now.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.220
Please, let Franchouchou perform!

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.510
Governor?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.390
I swear, this concert will help Saga!

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.840
It's for the sake of Saga! 
Saga will be revived!

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:30.830
You have to fix the Tosu area so people 
can make it to the Franchouchou show!

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.940
I'm begging you!

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.500
Okay, that's enough from—

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.040
I'm not talking to you!

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.640
What Saga needs right now is reassurance, 
for the heart of every single resident.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.820
We need something to unify us so
we can all tackle this disaster together...

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.680
Franchouchou can do that.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.370
Governor, please. Make the call.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.080
Man... What were you doing?

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.810
<b><i>Episode 12</i></b>

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.810
<b><i>The Greatest
 SAGA in History</i></b>

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:09.900
This is Tatsumi.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.910
It's Ookoba. I guess I 
finally got through...

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.340
<i>How have things gone on your end?</i>

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.990
Is that seriously the first 
thing you're gonna ask?

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.550
Do you realize the hoops I had to jump 
through to score a chopper ride up here?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.870
It's gonna be rough... Yeah, a charity 
concert sounds nice and all,

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.070
but when there are no guarantees that 
the show will actually come together,

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.930
it's not easy to convince 
people to get on board.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.500
<i>I believe you have what it takes.</i>

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.520
Don't be so sure! I haven't run in 
this neck of the woods in a decade.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.710
<i>I know you can do it.</i>

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.880
For the record, you haven't 
exactly earned my trust yet.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.180
I just...

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.780
I intend to do what I can

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.490
and let god sort out the rest.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.220
<i>I'm not leaving a damn thing up to god.</i>

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.990
<i>Not after all this time.</i>

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.520
I guess not...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.370
Mainichi Shinbun

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.800
Mainichi Shinbun

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.340
There's only a week until the concert.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.840
Yeah! I'm starting to get 
butterflies in my stomach!

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.190
It's a good kind of tension, though.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.200
We've all been really focused 
these last few days.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.310
Maybe more than ever before.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.480
I noticed that, as well!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.570
Me, too! I wonder why?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.400
My Tamagotchi, too!

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.080
Oyajitchi and Memetchi got 
mixed into a Memeoyajitchi!

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.200
Is that... really relevant?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.670
I'm tryin' to say we're on a roll!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.030
I wonder if he's watching us now...

00:03:58.490 --> 00:03:59.430
Who's that?

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.940
Someone I knew a long time ago.

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:10.790
I bet he's rooting for us! Just like Mommy.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:14.320
Yes.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:19.850
Now we've just got to put on a good 
performance to cheer Saga up on the day!

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.120
I hope people will be able to make it.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:27.320
Damn it, if it weren't for this whole mess, 
we'd be passing out fliers

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.760
and talking up the show on the radio...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.300
Huh.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.390
What day is it today?

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.610
The day? Uh...

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:40.000
Come to think of it, we've been paying more 
attention to the dates than what day it is.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.510
I think it's Friday, maybe?

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.770
Dude! That's the day we're on air!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.910
Crap, crap, crap, I've gotta get ready fast!

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.570
But with everything going on...

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.500
That's why I wanna do it!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.950
'Sides, we already missed a session!

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.060
No one can blame you for that. 
It was a literal disaster situation.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.290
Are you seriously gonna go?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.950
Damn right. If we don't go, 
then Saga's gonna lose itself.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.560
<b>FM Saga
Studio</b>

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.560
Oh, you've got the wrong day.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.900
It's actually Sunday.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.050
Our... Our mistake...

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.620
Girl... I'm gonna kill you...

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.830
Man, all seven of you are here, huh?

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.880
<b>FM Saga
Studio</b>

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.860
This actually works out! Since you're here, 
why don't you go on the air?

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.100
Is that okay?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:34.730
<b>FM Saga
Studio</b>

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:28.500
Yeah! We're all set to broadcast, but none 
of our regular personalities can make it in...

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:31.040
So we've been wondering what we could 
do other than just read the news.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.730
Honestly, there's no way to know how 
many people are even listening, but...

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.520
We don't mind!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.910
Thank you so much!

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.450
Thanks!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.620
<i>We'll continue to bring you updates 
on the affected areas going forward.</i>

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.390
<i>If you have any new information, 
feel free to contact us, as well.</i>

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.290
<i>Now, we actually have some wonderful 
guests in the studio today.</i>

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.760
<i>Good evening! We're Franchouchou!</i>

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.160
Diiing!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.670
Hey, Maimai's Franchouchou 
sense is tingling.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:59.670
Crank that radio up! Please! Radio! Louder!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.180
That's what I'd expect from a 
mega-fan and former member.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:05.460
<i>Well, to all the folks in Saga...</i>

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:11.340
Everybody, I think it's pretty rough 
out there for you all right now.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:16.570
And... I dunno how you're 
hearing me right now,

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:20.310
but I bet you've all got your worries, 
or might be feeling lonely...

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.890
Hell, you might just be pissed off 
about everything that's happened.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.440
But... I dunno how to put this...

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.850
<i>Right now, a lot of people are 
doing everything they can,</i>

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.820
<i>in all sorts of different ways, to help.</i>

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.800
<i>It was the same way for 
the shelter we stayed at.</i>

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:43.930
<i>And that's how you sorta get involved... 
and connect to people, I guess.</i>

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.030
<i>I dunno if I'm getting my point across,</i>

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.550
<i>but I think that kinda thing 
is a really big deal.</i>

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:56.260
<i>So, all of us in Franchouchou have thought 
about what we can do to help...</i>

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.230
All seven of us have 
talked this over, and...

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:05.950
In the end, we wanna connect to 
you all by singing and dancing.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.350
We want to cheer you on!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:11.330
That's why Franchouchou is going 
to be putting on a concert.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:16.260
<i>March 8th. At the Ekimae Fudosan Stadium!</i>

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.860
<i>A year ago, we seriously 
blew it at that same venue.</i>

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.980
<i>We drew a tiny crowd... panicked...</i>

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.690
<i>It was a real mess.</i>

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.740
<i>And, just like last time...</i>

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:34.940
<i>Nah, I think it's gonna be even 
harder to pull off than last time.</i>

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.700
But... all the same, we're going 
to put on the best show ever!

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:44.390
I know there are people who are gonna think 
that's crazy, with everything going on...

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:48.170
But if we... If by singing, we can...

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:52.620
I dunno if we'll really be able to 
help people feel better, but...

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:58.510
We're gonna be on stage, hoping we can 
make you smile, even just a little!

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:02.920
Because that's what being idols means to us!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:07.900
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:12.930
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.890
<b>March 7th, 2020</b>

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.970
Do you all have your things?

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.390
Yes!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.390
Right!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.390
Okay!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.610
We don't know how things will be out there,
 so let's be careful on the road.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.050
Hell, we're zombies. We'll be fine.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.430
That's true! We are zombies.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.070
Let's get going, then.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.440
<b>March 8th, 2020</b>

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.710
<i>On March 8th, sixteen days from now, 
you'll need to assemble at EFS at 10 a.m.</i>

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.400
Damn it, Shades! Did you get the date wrong?

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.680
I guess we weren't sure what 
day it was for a while there, too.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:03.130
I'm not gonna give up.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:06.200
No matter what.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.250
I don't care how bad it gets...

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:16.100
Even if we try our very hardest and it 
still goes badly, I'm gonna keep trying.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.120
Even if god tries to stop us! Or the devil!

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.950
Until we outlast everything that 
tries to get in the way...

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.600
I'm gonna keep at our revenge!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.630
Hey!

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:47.500
Those dudes are seriously awesome!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.090
I'm curious how they made 
it all the way out here.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.000
Ei-yah!

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.420
—chouchou!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.880
Ei-yah!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.400
—chouchou!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.720
Ei-yah!

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:17.770
—chouchou!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.950
Would you look at that?

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.850
I'm coming to you from the Ekimae 
Fudosan Stadium in Saga,

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:30.470
where the damage caused by 
flooding is still visible.

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:36.410
A massive crowd is gathering for a charity 
concert by the idol group Franchouchou!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:42.200
We at NBK Fukuoka caught up with 
them at a shelter a week ago,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.990
and the response from our 
viewers was massive!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.360
Not only that, but newspapers with 
circulation throughout the country

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:51.820
have been publishing ads for the show, 
raising the event's profile even higher.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.690
<b>Trending in Japan 

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.680
Social media has also been abuzz 
with talk of the concert

00:11:56.050 --> 00:12:00.560
after posts from Shiori Baba-san from Iron Frill, 
one of Japan's biggest idol groups,

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.530
as well as the actor Light Oozora-san.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:08.260
It looks like the arena still isn't 
ready for the show just yet.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:12.790
In spite of that, you can see how many 
have assembled here today to support Saga!

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.790
With the notoriety brought from 
national exposure in five big papers,

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.640
businesses from all over the country, 
starting with Saga's own Hisanaka Pharmaceuticals,

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.330
have volunteered to help sponsor the event.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.620
And it's not just Japan, either!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.500
People from a variety of 
countries are offering aid

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:31.900
after hearing about the disaster in Kyushu!

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:36.260
Like I told you... The answer 
can be found in Saga!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:40.050
We are seeing the world 
come together for Saga...

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:43.820
no, Japan, in a way rarely 
seen throughout history!

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:48.700
You might even call it an epic... saga!

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.510
Thank you so much.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.020
Just so we're clear here...

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:02.310
All we've done is choose to prioritize the most 
effective strategy, after logical consideration.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:03.930
Tatsumi-kun.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.980
Saga's not giving up.

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:21.050
Saga!

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:26.080
Revenge!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.000
<b>Franchouchou 
Green Room</b>

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.880
<i>There's no turning back the clock, 
just facing what's happened</i>

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.970
<i>Take those past glories 
and leave them be</i>

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:15.680
<i>Just hang on tight</i>

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.810
<i>Never give up again</i>

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:21.270
<i>If you wanna make sure 
your loss has meaning</i>

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.020
<i>Get on your feet</i>

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:22.980
<i>Shake yourself off</i>

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.520
<i>No matter how battered you are</i>

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.440
<i>After swallowing the pain</i>

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.400
<i>Could you stand up again?</i>

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.160
<i>Why worry about when to give up?</i>

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.780
<i>Do you really want to go out on a whimper?</i>

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.580
<i>Bet on a comeback</i>

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.950
<i>No matter how many times you fall</i>

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.040
<i>Take deferred and stockpiled dreams</i>

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.540
<i>And shout them out!</i>

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:53.260
<i>Even if it's a fight with no chance to win</i>

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.510
<i>That doesn't change the dream 
or how bad you want it!</i>

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:57.930
<i>The disappointment</i>

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:58.810
<i>of failure,</i>

00:15:58.810 --> 00:15:59.730
<i>the mistakes</i>

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:00.600
<i>and regrets</i>

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.810
<i>can all be thrown into the fire 
that signals a new start!</i>

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:11.070
<i>Even if the whole world gives up on you, 
keep fighting as long as you breathe!</i>

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:11.990
<i>The will</i>

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>and the passion</i>

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.860
<i>To return</i>

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:14.660
<i>and fight back</i>

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:22.120
<i>Are what you need to shine 
bright and blaze on!</i>

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>If it's an end where you've 
spent all you've had to give</i>

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:39.350
<i>Even if the world's finally shown you mercy</i>

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.810
<i>What kind of life is it</i>

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:49.020
<i>Without some scars in the end?</i>

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:53.780
<i>Even if it's a fight with no chance to win</i>

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:57.200
<i>Our hearts will never stop blazing</i>

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.410
<i>Atone for</i>

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.330
<i>your surrender</i>

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.200
<i>Retract your</i>

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.040
<i>retreat and</i>

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:01.910
<i>plan for</i>

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:02.830
<i>the revolution</i>

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:03.710
<i>Rejoin and</i>

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:04.620
<i>start again</i>

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.500
<i>The disappointment</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.380
<i>of failure,</i>

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.330
<i>the mistakes</i>

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:08.130
<i>and regrets</i>

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:12.970
<i>can all be thrown into the fire 
that signals a new start!</i>

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:20.260
<i>Even if the whole world gives up on you, 
keep fighting as long as you breathe!</i>

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.390
<i>The will</i>

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.430
<i>and the passion</i>

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.270
<i>To return</i>

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.180
<i>and fight back</i>

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:31.230
<i>Are what you need to shine 
bright and blaze on!</i>

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.230
<i></i>

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:28.180
Fran... Franchouchou!

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:32.010
<i></i>

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.550
Franchouchou!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.050
Number Zero!

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:52.830
<i>Let's sing of this day</i>

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:58.260
<i>Shining bright!</i>

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:04.740
<i>(Still Alive!)</i>

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:10.460
<i>I looked outward, with eyes full 
of disappointment and regret</i>

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:14.710
<i>And then I threw away my mirror</i>

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:20.470
<i>Because when it comes to the 
meaning of happiness and beauty</i>

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:24.720
<i>I won't let other people choose them</i>

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.520
<i>Tear apart your idea of normal</i>

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:30.020
<i>Embrace what makes you unique</i>

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.690
<i>And then don't look back 
as you let it loose!</i>

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:38.780
<i>Living out a miracle with 
every fiber of my being</i>

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:42.490
<i>Even if you run away or get scared</i>

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.450
<i>(Even crawling around)</i>

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.620
<i>At the center of the world</i>

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.750
<i>Imperfect as you might be now, carry on</i>

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.420
<i>You can take pride in what makes you strange</i>

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.500
<i>(Fully exposed to see)</i>

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.710
<i>And take a bite into happiness</i>

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.010
<i>As the blessings come</i>

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.760
<i>Raining from above</i>

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.260
<i>Let's soak them up as we carry on</i>

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.510
<i>Let there be light</i>

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:09.140
<i>So you can reach the glory</i>

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:14.900
<i>And cast your gaze upward, 
upward, never stopping!</i>

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.510
<i>Come on now!</i>

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.980
Thank you!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.500
<i>Let there be light</i>

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:41.130
<i>Escaping the darkness! Believing in the wind!</i>

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.430
<i>Marching to an exit from despair</i>

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.510
<i>Let there be light</i>

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.720
<i>Where we can breathe easy</i>

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.180
<i>Where we'll live</i>

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:54.350
<i>Free to shine on, shine on, without a stop!</i>

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:58.270
<i>Shining!</i>

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:12.300
Encore! Encore! Encore!

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:14.110
You've done an amazing job
 in a dire situation.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.540
But... still, though! Don't get 
the wrong idea! You still—

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.080
It's still too early to 
consider ourselves winners.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.970
Even this EFS show is nothing 
more than a milestone.

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:35.440
There's still a great deal 
more for us to do, right?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.340
And I know we can shine even brighter!

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:42.160
After all, Franchouchou is eternal
and unstoppable, right?

00:21:43.410 --> 00:21:47.940
We're the idol zombies who will always keep 
fighting, no matter when, no matter where!

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:03.470
Kotaro-san?

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:06.200
What? Why are you apologizing?

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:09.270
He's convulsing! 
Should we call an ambulance?

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:11.850
Wait, maybe he's doing that mudskipper—

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:12.930
I'm crying, okay?!

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.150
I'm crying!

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.670
I'm a grown-ass man and I'm crying!

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:25.540
What's with you, huh?!

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:29.830
Where do a bunch of wimpy zombies get 
off trying to sound so confident?!

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:35.420
You think those half-rotten throats 
should be spouting nonsense at me?!

00:22:35.930 --> 00:22:40.680
Just so you know, 
Saga's barely even a little saved!

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:51.180
<b>Franchouchou Green Room</b>

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:46.050
Got it?! So go and hit 
the crowd with your soul!

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:47.980
Hell yeah!

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:49.790
Go, go, go, go, go!

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.230
Go, go, go!

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:17.540
<i>It's not like anything's gonna change</i>

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.330
<i>But it's not like we're gonna give up</i>

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:26.170
<i>It must be because there's 
still some hope left</i>

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:31.800
<i>I may not have the answers 
that I wanted the most</i>

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:37.770
<i>Travelers! Looks like our 
smiles are peeking through!</i>

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:42.350
<i>You can wrap them in a blanket</i>

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:48.690
<i>But it seems our dreams will just spill out</i>

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:54.950
<i>Why not keep dreaming even 
after springing awake?</i>

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:00.540
<i>Let's set out anew and say good morning!</i>

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:06.300
<i>Maybe my one small step 
is enough to reach someone</i>

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:12.010
<i>If that's the kind of future we can have...</i>

00:24:12.010 --> 00:24:17.560
<i>Then that's where I am headed now, 
even with dark clouds in the way</i>

00:24:17.560 --> 00:24:26.520
<i>We're all in the same boat anyway, 
so let's head there together</i>

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:29.190
<i>Let's make it happen!</i>

00:24:49.670 --> 00:24:55.300
<i>Embracing the world around 
me that's so full of wishes</i>

00:24:55.300 --> 00:25:01.020
<i>And heading straight into the future</i>

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:09.440
<i>Maybe my one small step 
is enough to reach someone</i>

00:25:09.440 --> 00:25:15.070
<i>If that's the kind of future we can have...</i>

00:25:15.070 --> 00:25:20.790
<i>Then that's where I am headed now, 
even with dark clouds in the way</i>

00:25:20.790 --> 00:25:29.630
<i>We're all in the same boat anyway, 
so let's head there together</i>

00:25:30.380 --> 00:25:31.960
<i>Let's make it happen!</i>

00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:37.960
All together!

00:25:42.190 --> 00:25:46.730
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah!</i>

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:51.570
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah!</i>

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:43.160
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>
